WEBVTT

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:35.740
Well, Miss Peach Maki has finished filming
"Miracle" in the role of Oume!

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:41.330
Maki, you did really great.
You were perfect for the character you played.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.410
Next time, appear as a guest on my TV drama.

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.370
Oh? You really mean it?

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:48.040
I'd love to! In what role?

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.000
"As a clumsy magical girl"?!

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.380
What is a Magical Girl?

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.760
Maki, I went ahead and formally accepted the offer.
A magical girl is... A magical girl is... A magical girl is...

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.770
Hey, hey, hey now. Manager, is it gonna be alright?

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:06.480
Will what be alright?

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.810
AGE-WISE I CAN BARELY PULL IT OFF! JUST BARELY!

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.730
OR PERHAPS I'M ALREADY A BIT TOO OLD!

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:17.570
Even being Olive in Chinese Angels
was really pushing it, so for playing a magical girl...

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.200
isn't middle-school-aged the oldest you can be?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.580
I'm also conscious of how dated my expressions are...

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:26.450
You've got a youthful face
and you're still plenty young - you'll be fine.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.000
I-is that right?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.750
Yeah, this clumsy magical girl's an iffy character
who's barely pulling it off age-wise, so you're fine.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.550
Hearing that hurts in its own special way!

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.630
Memorize the spells so you
can say them without stumbling.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.840
MAGICAL
GIRL
THREE
SEVEN

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:39.840
Uh... okay.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.510
Spells, huh? I used to play around with those a lot.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.100
Stuff like Miracle Holy something or other...

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.020
I CAN'T READ ANY OF THIS!

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.150
You've gotta study.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:53.400
My linguistic ability isn't the problem here!

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:56.440
The backstory says she came from the Valley of Witches,

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.900
but do real magical girls
use these kind of sutra-esque spells?!

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.950
Maki, you alright?

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:04.620
Mr. Comer!

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.500
Congratulations on your first film appearance.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.960
M-Mr. Hozuki?!

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:16.170
Hozuki, if you don't mind, will you look at the camera
and say "Miracle is the best" together with Maki?

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:19.630
NOW SHOWING TO RAVE REVIEWS

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.090
I'm gonna use it in a commercial, you see.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.630
Not a chance.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:24.800
Well, Maki, you're doing your best. I will go see "Miracle."

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.770
Wait... what are you two doing together anyway?

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.440
We're having a meeting about a DVD
for breeding goldfish plants.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:37.230
Mr. Comer isn't just the head of the judges' panel
for the goldfish plant contest, he's the event's founder.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:42.070
Having a hit director film your plant-breeding DVD...
What kind of connections does this guy have?

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.950
Maki, next you're gonna play a magical girl, right?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:49.080
You know, the one who's designing
the costume is little... old... me.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:51.370
Ah, I suppose that's a relief.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:56.250
Ever since Mr. Comer started designing my costumes
it's certainly true I've gotten more fans.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.210
You're going to play a magical girl?

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.380
Uh... y-yes...

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:01.840
Oh? You don't want to?

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:03.550
No, it's not like that!

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.760
But, do you think spells like these are okay?

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.100
They're fine - the character's
supposed to be surreal, after all.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:09.770
"Fine," he says...

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.640
I'd really like to meet a real one once, though...

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.690
Mr. Hozuki, do you know any witches?

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:20.030
I don't know any myself,
but how about I try asking Lady Lilith?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.780
I'm Magical Marin from the Valley of Witches.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.570
NO WAY! SHE FOR REAL?!

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:30.080
That Lilith girl summoned me here all of a sudden...

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.290
If you got any questions, hurry up and ask 'em.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:37.290
Leaving aside magical girls,
I can't believe a witch like this exists nowadays!

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.250
Hey, please autograph this!

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:43.380
Is "Magical" your name? Or is "Marin"?
Not that I like either of them...

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:49.760
You sure are rude. I'm a friend of that witch
who tricked Snow White, you know.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.770
You're not the actual witch who did it, right?!

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.560
What is your relation to Lady Lilith?

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.480
We are work and tea pals.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:02.690
At any rate, my house is made of sweets,
so I get lots of guests.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:05.950
I'm renting the place that my friend
used to live in, you see.

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:09.580
The security deposit was high, but it's a nice property.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:12.250
My friend got burned to death by Gretel, though.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:16.080
You sure are friends with many people
involved in major incidents.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.790
So, what would you like to ask?

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.340
All kinds of stuff about witches.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:23.340
I want a reference point for my drama's line
between reality and fiction.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.800
Hmm, what kind of story is it?

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:33.310
Note: Lumonde, Elise, and Alfort  are all sweets sold by the brand "Bourbon."
With Queen Sylbeine's life on the line, Lum*nde,

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:33.310
El*se, and Al*ort fight to protect the country.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.390
The country they protect...
that must be the Kingdom of Bourbon.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.940
Note: White Rollita.
Maki will be playing the
clumsy apprentice witch, White *llita.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:46.530
To say nothing of the clumsy part, I have a feeling
the whole "White *llita" name is real stretch...

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:50.870
Why? I'm telling you it'll be alright. It's best
if the character comes across as sour anyway.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:54.290
Why go out of your way to make
the character clumsy in the first place?

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:59.710
It's a plot device with the idea that a girl who's prone
to making lots of mistakes is more charming.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:03.050
Ah, well in that case I'm a clumsy girl, too.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:07.380
I'm constantly breaking dishes
and mishearing things, you see.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.260
I hate to be rude,
but isn't that simply because you're old?

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:13.810
Huh?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:18.560
I usually also cause explosions
when I'm making witches' medicines.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.270
Realistically speaking, isn't that a problem?

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.440
Well, aren't you annoying! I've been
a clumsy witch like this for over 300 years now.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.860
I've got a well-seasoned kind of cuteness!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.490
I'd say at this point you're just an adult
who makes careless mistakes.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.160
Is that right?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:39.290
Today I burned my hotcakes and on top of that,
I fell down and exposed my underpants.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.040
That fits the definition of "clumsy," right?

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:45.300
Isn't that what you want from me?

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.970
You may be clumsy, but that's not what I'm looking for.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:49.970
What I'd like to see you to do is...

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:54.640
cackle with laughter as you fly atop a broomstick,
make frog soup, and so on.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:07:00.770
Ah... I'm no good at flying on brooms
and I can't stand frogs.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:05.360
How disappointing! So then
what is it that makes you a witch?!

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:12.070
Well, right now I'm single and just like Tinker Bell,
so I'm counted as fully-fledged sorcerer.

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:13.950
THAT kind of sorcerer, huh?!

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:19.160
Every year I bring a sacrifice with me
and go to Satan's Castle and work, you see.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.500
And that's how I got to know Lilith.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.210
She didn't tell you that?

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:31.090
I see. Leaving aside magic and the like, witches
were at first a hard-core orthodox sect of devils, huh?

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:35.350
Also, originally witches flew in the sky atop baskets.
That's the old way of doing it.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.680
I do know how to fly inside one of those, you know.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:43.690
If you really think about it, Lady Lilith herself
is a veteran devil, isn't she?

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:48.530
Well, there are all kinds of witches
- I lean toward devil myself.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.490
Fascinating stuff.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:54.410
Ms. Marin, would you care
to take Maki's place as the magical girl?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.580
Maki, this time I'm gonna have to cancel
your appearance. Sorry, my bad.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:58.870
HUH?!

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.580
The film industry is far more...

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.750
...Devilish...

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:07.710
I'll pass. And besides, there's somewhere
I want to go, you see.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.760
SANBAN SHIBORI BEER

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.760
KANEKO
IRONWORKS

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.390
EDOGAWA
MANGETSU

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.100
Ni hao. Konnichiwa.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:21.810
Greetings.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:25.650
Are you running short
of any natural remedies or medicines?

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.980
Yeah, red spider lily. Top me off.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.820
Seems like the kind of place that sells gremlins.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:39.910
I know dodgy pharmacies like this have around
for a long time, but they sure are sketchy, huh?

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.000
The Mundane World also has its various needs, after all.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.710
There's quiet demand in the Mundane World, too.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:48.250
Ah, see?

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:51.090
A human customer who's engaged
in a particular business just walked in.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:52.210
Excuse me!

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:57.050
He's extremely suspicious-looking,
but he must be the real deal if he's coming here...

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:01.180
AM I PRETTY?

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:58.970
A monster customer.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:01.020
Ah, it's the Slit Mouth Woman!

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.390
It's a god customer.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:04.940
Note: A pharmaceutical product for acne, rough skin, and mouth ulcers.
Chocola *B, please.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.940
Note: Matsukiyo, short for Matsumoto Kiyoshi, a major drug store chain.
Buy that kind of thing at Matsu*yo.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:11.900
Also, I heard some underground rumors
about overseas shaman and witches and such.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.320
Ah, look who just walked in!

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:17.620
Please show me all of your Eastern herbs.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.580
No way! Are you serious?!

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:23.250
Miss Maki had that same reaction.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.500
You again! Stay away from pharmacies!

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:29.000
Before returning home, Ms. Marin said
she'd like to do some sightseeing in Japan,

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.880
while taking the opportunity to do some inspections.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.260
So there really are witches...

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:38.550
Witches are pros when it comes to medicine.
Pharmacists around the world follow their example.

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:42.970
Anyway, I want to see lots of different medicines
from both that world and this one.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.810
I already had a look inside Matsu*yo.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.980
Shiro, are you here to inspect this place, too?

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:49.980
You sure seem to follow Mr. Hozuki everywhere...

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.860
What's the matter? Shiro...

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:58.070
Ah, Shiro... It's fine if you speak now.

00:09:58.450 --> 00:09:59.530
Huh? Really?

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:05.330
Today I'm on luggage-carrying duty! As a dog,
I'm the only one who it's okay for to go to the big city.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:09.380
Even if it's just barely okay for monkeys to come,
I hear that there's no way pheasants can.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:11.170
JUST
BARELY

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.130
I-indeed...

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.340
Pheasants, you know...

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.760
Tell Rurio that we'll head to the forest
together sometime soon...

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.760
Note: Maihama is the location of Tokyo Disney Resort.
After this I'd like to head to Maihama.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.640
For starters, you'd definitely get mistaken
for a cast member.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:26.770
Wouldn't her clothing be partly to blame for that?

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:27.940
I would think so.

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:32.270
On a related note, mind if I ask you about a trivial matter?

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:35.110
What's this all of a sudden...? Go ahead.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:37.740
Where'd that old geezer buy his clothes?

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.160
Ah, now he's done it...

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:43.830
Note: Districts in Tokyo known for having a high population of elderly people.
That's the kind of fashion you often see
around Asakusa and Shibamata, isn't it?

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:47.910
What?! I don't want any advice
from a guy who's always clad in all black!

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:52.040
So why did you choose that combination of colors?

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.170
ADZUKI BEAN COLOR

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:50.420
SUPER DEEP KHAKI

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.040
BLAH GREY
SUPER DEEP KHAKI

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:52.960
GREY
BLAH GREY
SUPER DEEP KHAKI

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:56.880
When I heard he was going
to mundane world looking like that,

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:00.840
Note: A game similar to croquet, quite popular with the elderly in Japan.
I instinctively thought he must be going there
to play gateball or something.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.050
Huh? My outfit is... strange?

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:06.430
More than strange, I'd say it feels out of place.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.140
Especially since you look young physically speaking.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:13.900
On the Mundane World's news this morning,
they had a feature on active old men,

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:16.530
and there was a guy with the exact same outfit as you.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:22.490
It's almost scary how good he is
at selecting presents to give to girls, and yet...

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:25.990
Why is your fashion sense so abysmal?

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:29.330
Shut up! This's better than putting
way too much effort into it!

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.210
That reminds me, his drawings are also catastrophic.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.460
Maybe there's something peculiar about his right brain...

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:35.880
In short...

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:41.550
this divine beast's power of expression
is abysmally absent when it comes to design.
Meow, meow, meow...

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:42.970
Ah, that's it.
Meow, meow, meow...

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:48.310
I bet your taste in women is determined by your
enormous databases and miraculous intuition.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.140
Essentially, he's a math and science type of guy.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.980
As a woman, here's my opinion...

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.020
Huh? Uh, okay.

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:59.320
The accent color someone chooses,
really says a lot about their taste.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:02.240
Ma'am, you have zero accent colors.

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:05.370
I'm not a "ma'am" - I'm a miss.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.330
For real?!

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:11.000
Perhaps the both of you would be better off
with new outfits for the Mundane World.

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:16.210
Fine, I get it! Come back here in two hours!
I'll show you some fantastic fashion sense!

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:19.590
That's the kind of line someone
with actual taste would never say... you know.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:20.670
Shut up!

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:24.840
It's been two hours!

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:26.890
Alright, Miss Marin is up first.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:36.980
She just went from looking like a character
from a certain Land to one from Ghi*li.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:40.150
No question she'd be good
at making stuff like stew and cookies.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:44.070
Note: Brands of Japanese stew and cookies, respectively.
Seems like Aunt Crea and Aunt Stella
would be among her nieces.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:46.740
Note: Beard Papa, a brand of cream puffs.
Don't forget  Bear* Papa.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:50.910
Well, she's a Westerner, so I suppose her outfit is fine.

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.290
Now, let's see how the old man fairs.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:01.670
Ouch!

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:05.760
Note: Yuji Oda, a popular leading man in the 90s known for his flashy fashion.
Even the Y*ji Oda of 20 years ago wasn't this trendy!

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:09.050
Then stop being a poor loser,
you damn year-round funeral-goer!

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:12.730
In some sense, I prefer your good ol' white coat...

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:15.310
It did seem like it was your turn
to serve school lunches, though.

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:18.440
Uniforms have a way of concealing many things.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:23.610
The same goes for my robe. It's convenient
not having to think about what to wear.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:27.530
I also always wear the same thing,
and to be honest it is convenient.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:30.240
How should I put, young man...

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:36.540
You and this Chief of Staff here have similar faces,
so wouldn't wearing similar clothes suit you?

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:39.040
Wai...! Don't say that!

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:41.000
Absolutely not!

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.380
I find it awkward even when I'm wearing something
similar to a stranger on the train.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:47.470
Please don't wear something from
the same brand as me in a different color.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:51.390
I won't! Your own taste
is quite questionable, you know!

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.850
Where the hell did you buy something
with such a strange pattern?

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.560
On the contrary, I don't want to bequeath
even one ounce of my flawless taste to you!

00:13:57.560 --> 00:14:00.610
No one said anything about that! You trendy geezer!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:04.740
Where do you get that confidence from anyway?

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:06.610
It's a bit scary, really...

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.280
THE AGE
OF EASTERN

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.280
MEDICINE
FOR PETS
LARGEST DOMESTIC
TOY SHOW OPENS
INCREASED INTEREST
IN INTELLECTUAL
TRAINING TOYS

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.370
Hey, you...

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:14.620
MAGES
CHINESE ANGELS

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.330
Wear what ya want...

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:18.420
For some reason, I feel like we've lost...

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:24.090
In the Mundane World, children's clothing
has gotten super cute as of late.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:26.380
They even have shops that specialize in in.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:38.690
Indulging in Western Clothing

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:40.520
"Clothes"...?

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:43.360
Nothing suits you two better than those kimonos.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:44.860
We'd like some Western clothes.

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:47.820
Even when I was in the Mundane World,
I was thinking how nice that would be.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:50.660
Stuff that's nothing like what
a traditional Japanese doll wears.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.030
Note: In spite of being Japan's first Prime Minister, Hirobumi Ito does not
have his face on any currency.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.030
I'll even pay with a Hirobumi Ito.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:55.200
Here are my treasured Edo-period copper coins.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.910
There's no real need for you to worry about paying...

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.790
We want something cute.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.330
Something that's not like
what Japanese dolls are dressed in.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.590
And you'd like me to go and buy some?

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:06.590
That would be quite a venture.

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:15.390
Fine, I'll go buy some, but don't get your hopes up.

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:25.520
If you're dissatisfied, go on and tell me.
You won't hurt my feelings.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:27.280
Not at all...

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.900
Thank you...

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.360
How admirable of them.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:37.450
Excuse me, Mr. Hozuki... Just say the word
and I'd be happy to go buy some.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.200
I'm trying to educate them.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:42.580
Now they see what happens
when you let a man pick out your clothes.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:46.590
Is he saying that to gloss over the fact
he really has no sense of fashion,

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:51.010
or did he buy that stuff on purpose
because he's trying to be hard on them?

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.380
With a guy like him, it's hard to tell...

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:58.310
Telling two young girls to state
their discontent takes a lot of courage.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:02.100
Having little girls point that kind of thing
out stabs you right in the heart, after all.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:05.690
Still, those childish outfits are pretty cute.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.690
They're kinda heartwarming, you know?

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:12.240
Even if adults think they look cute,
those two themselves don't like them one bit.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.030
I had something like that happen a long time ago...

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:21.460
I was given a kimono by my beloved Grandma,
and I couldn't bear to say anything. I just really couldn't.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.210
It was this iffy purplish red...

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:27.710
But, I really do love my Grandma.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:30.210
Oh, the way I felt at the time...!

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:34.050
I don't have any relatives,
so I can't understand that kind of thing myself.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:36.760
Look at those eyes, Mr. Hozuki...

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:40.350
They're like haniwa clay figures
filled with a mix of discretion and sorrow.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:44.480
I've given them a chance to learn about courtesy
and putting on a facade.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:47.020
Now, please go and grant them their dream.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:51.990
Well then, I'll buy them one more outfit...
and leave the selection up to you, Miss O-Koh.

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:55.860
IT'S A CRIME!

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:56.820
By the way, when you went to the Mundane World
before, you wore snake-print clothing...

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.530
What was the deciding factor on that?

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:02.540
That was simply... me thinking
"snake-print would be nice..."

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:05.170
Ah, that won't do. I can't
place my trust in on your sense of style.

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.420
How about you, Karauri?

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:11.050
I look at magazines
and buy the featured top and bottom sets.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:12.630
I go with my gut feeling.

00:17:12.840 --> 00:17:17.470
But, no matter who you ask to go,
I think there's one fundamental problem...

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:22.850
Those twins have doll-like faces, so I don't think
anything too casual would suit them very well.

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:29.020
Good point. But those two themselves,
want to break free from looking like Japanese dolls.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:32.440
How about using the Mirror of Johari
to look at people in the Mundane World

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:34.110
and decide what direction to go in?

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:38.160
Once in a while you make an astute suggestion, Nasubi.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.120
Where should we view?

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.500
Let's go with that Land place... Plenty of kids there.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.790
There are lots of kids wearing cute clothes.

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:52.750
There are also cosplayers among them,
so it's actually rather hard to get a good idea.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:54.420
Lots of adults there, too.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.470
Ah, that person who just walked by was really striking!

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:02.640
Oh, I see there are some people
with crazy hair just like demons.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:06.560
And going in the same direction as that guy's taste
in clothing might be unexpectedly interesting.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:08.020
I know him.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:08.690
Huh?

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.150
Ah! Oh?!

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:12.980
You're right. Isn't he King Shinko's Chief of Staff?!

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:16.610
Moreover, he's not really even a demon
- more of an eminent historical figure.

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:18.700
Think he's there doing an inspection?

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:19.950
Probably...

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:23.490
Chiefs of Staff do periodically
go the Mundane World, after all.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:27.580
He certainly sticks out, but those clothes
do suit him better than regular ones would.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:32.500
Instead of observing, I think maybe
he's just there to have a good time.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:38.590
Or rather, taking a good look, I see that next
to Takamura is King Sotai's Chief of Staff, Misohagi.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:43.510
Ah... He's also wearing some rather fitting clothes...

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:48.640
A gray hoodie and jeans...
Hmm, he has a low-key fashion sense, doesn't he?

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:54.190
More than taste, it comes down to us Chiefs of Staff
disguising ourselves so as to not seem out of place.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:58.860
Most likely, the woman next to him
is King Gokan's Chief of Staff, Shikimi.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.870
Her disguise is perfect!

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:10.330
Please take a good look.
There's a school emblem on her socks...

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:13.540
She's playing the part of a mother using the
small accessories of her daughter's school uniform

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.000
so that they don't go to waste.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.300
It's a minor detail, but moms like that,
are definitely out there!

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:19.380
I've got it.

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:24.510
It's tough to head to an amusement park on your own,
so they've all gone together for an inspection.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.810
What's with this community
of Chiefs of Staff of the Ten Kings?

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:33.770
In any case, having them chose clothes
for the Zashiki Warashi might be a mistake...

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:36.110
Yeah, I'd say so.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:40.650
Well, I just thought of this now,
but how about asking Mr. Comer?

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:43.780
Big bang!

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:49.830
He may not look it, but that's he's the designer
for Hell's number one brand, Comer×Comer.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.830
I can't ask him to do something like that for free.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:59.550
Hmm... I do know someone who
strangely understands what girls like...

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:04.720
Ah, I think I have an idea of who you mean,
but he's out of the question.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:11.560
Well, it's not that he has good taste
- he simply has plentiful data.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:15.770
To that celestial maiden,
I'd give a collar to adorn her cat's neck.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:19.650
To that fox spirit, I'd give a ruby birthstone ring.

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:23.660
For that Hell Minion, I think maybe
a Comer×Comer handbag would be good.

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:27.200
It's a skill he's picked up using
the minimum amount of experience points.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:33.080
But, you know, that guy gives gifts that are exactly
what girls want deep down in their hearts.

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:34.460
On top of that...

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.290
I really can't decide between these two...

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:40.340
When he hears a girl wavering like that...

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.550
The one you choose is the epitome of good taste.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:46.510
That's what he says. Pretty amazing, right?

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:48.560
He can get lost.

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:53.600
But, if you leave it to him, they might end up
with Chinese-esque outfits.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.730
Well, he is from a foreign country, after all.

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.270
"Foreign country"?

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:00.860
That's right. Western attire
is foreign clothing in the first place.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:03.530
It's not the apparel of the Mundane World's Japan.

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:11.950
Hi! How are you? I've brought
lots of children's clothes with me.

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:15.420
We should've just asked her in the first place, huh?

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:18.670
I pilfered Lord Satan's collection, too.

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:20.710
That guy's kind of gross.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.550
So, where are the twins?

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:24.590
Over there.

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:27.590
I see...

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:31.010
Just leave it to me! I'll pick something out that suits them.

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:33.980
Oh my, how cute!

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:35.020
The twins got some new clothes.

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:35.940
The twins got some new clothes.
That's right.

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:37.190
I wonder if they were able to shed
their Japanese-doll-like appearances.

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:39.020
I wonder if they were able to shed
their Japanese-doll-like appearances.
Now tie it.

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:39.820
Now tie it.

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:41.570
How'd their outfits turn out?

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:47.360
THEY'RE FRENCH DOLLS!

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:54.330
In the end, maybe looking at a magazine and buying
a featured top and bottom set is the way to go...

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.840
NEXT TIME
ON HOZUKI'S
COOLHEADEDNESS...

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:29.550
Next time, an inattentive Otama
and a no-good female teacher!

00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:29.260
AND

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:31.840
You mean Uka-no-Mitama and Dakini-ten.

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:31.970
BUT

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:34.010
They're watching over everyone
from under the sod, right?

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:34.050
SO

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:37.270
Waiting for people's time of death, they have
their sights set on the moment they can feast.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.810
WE PRESENT:
DAKINI OF THE
WELCOMING COMMITTEE
AND
UNDER THE SOD
PLEASE ENJOY!

00:23:37.270 --> 00:23:39.600
A cat in full fling, huh?! Woof, woof!
